---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
export const page = { door: "this-month", topic: "money", label: "Money help", summary: "Can't pay a bill, behind on rent, cash fast, free tax help" };
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base title="Can't pay a bill? Money help in Morgantown and Mon County" description="Start with what is happening: you cannot pay a bill, you are behind on rent, you need cash fast, or you want free tax help. Local phone numbers and sources.">
  <h1>Can't pay a bill this month?</h1>
  <p class="lede">Call the company before the due date and ask for a payment plan. Then call 211. Pick what is happening to you below. Real help never charges a fee to apply.</p>

  <h2>I can't pay a bill this month</h2>
  <p>Start with your heat, water or electric bill: <a href={`${base}/utility-bills/`}>Help paying a utility bill</a>. It lists who to call first, with phone numbers and programs.</p>
  <p>For any other bill, call the company and say you cannot pay in full. Ask what payment plans they have. If you are not sure where to turn, call <a href="tel:211">211</a>, text your ZIP code to 898211, or visit <a href="https://wv211.org">wv211.org</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="rent">I'm behind on rent or facing eviction</h2>
  <p>We are still building our housing page. Until then, call <a href="tel:211">211</a> and say you are behind on rent. They can point you to local help. Keep any notice from your landlord or the court, and do not ignore it.</p>

  <h2>I need cash fast and I'm thinking about a payday loan</h2>
  <p>The West Virginia Division of Financial Institutions says traditional payday lenders are generally prohibited in this state. An online lender that offers one anyway is a warning sign. Before you borrow from anyone, call the Division at <a href="tel:3045582294">304-558-2294</a> and ask if the lender is allowed to lend here.</p>
  <p>Cheaper first steps: ask your biller for a payment plan, and call 211 about emergency help with the bill itself.</p>

  <h2>I want free help filing my taxes</h2>
  <p><strong>Christian Help</strong>, downtown Morgantown, offers free basic tax return preparation by trained, IRS-certified volunteers.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Call to book:</strong> <a href="tel:3042960221">304-296-0221</a></li>
    <li><strong>When:</strong> Wednesdays, 9 a.m. to 2 p.m., through April 1 (from the January 2026 article; the 2027 season dates are not published yet, so call to ask)</li>
    <li><strong>Who:</strong> households that earned $67,000 or less in 2025 may qualify (that was last season's limit; ask for this season's)</li>
    <li><strong>Bring:</strong> a photo ID for each person who earned money, Social Security numbers and birth dates for everyone on the return, last year's returns if you have them, W-2 and 1099 forms, and bank details if you want direct deposit. If you file together, both spouses come.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What things cost here</h2>
  <p>We have not found a trusted, sourced list of local rent, child care or pay figures yet, so we do not show numbers. We would rather show nothing than a guess. Know a public source? <a href="https://github.com/david-shortman/mon-county-community-hub/issues/new?template=suggest-resource.yml">Tell us</a>.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>Watch for scams.</strong> No government program pays your bills for a fee. Anyone who asks you to pay to apply, or to pay by gift card, wire or crypto, is a scam. Real help does not ask you to pay it. Report scams at <a href="https://reportfraud.ftc.gov">reportfraud.ftc.gov</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="meta">Sources, checked October 29, 2026: <a href="https://morgantownmag.com/get-free-help-filing-your-taxes/">Morgantown Magazine, free tax help (January 14, 2026)</a>, <a href="https://dfi.wv.gov/consumers">WV Division of Financial Institutions, consumers</a>, <a href="https://consumer.ftc.gov/consumer-alerts/2017/01/government-program-pays-your-bills">FTC, "Government program pays your bills?"</a>, and <a href="https://wv211.org">WV 211</a>. Something out of date? <a href="https://github.com/david-shortman/mon-county-community-hub/issues/new?template=suggest-resource.yml">Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
